{%- comment -%}
  Collection Product Card (`opc-`) — COLLECTION SECTIONS ONLY.
  The product card of Featured Collection, Collection Tabs and Category
  Collections (their Collection blocks render it; their shells load its
  stylesheet). It is not a general product card: other product surfaces keep
  snippets/product-card.liquid. Keeping one card across the collection family
  is what lets every one of those sections share the same card shapes.

  The product image fills the card; the title, an optional price and an add to
  cart button sit on a plate laid over its lower edge. Long titles stay on one
  line and end in an ellipsis.

  Look is chosen by data attributes, read from the card itself OR any ancestor —
  the second is how a parent block styles cards that a child block renders, since
  a child cannot pass its parent's settings on:
  - data-opc-plate  'tint' (default) — the card colour rising from the bottom
                    'glass'          — frosted glass in the card colour, no border
                    'solid'          — the card colour; always floats
  - data-opc-float  present — the plate floats: inset from the card's edges
                    with its own rounded corners (glass only; solid always does)
  - data-opc-cart   'fixed' (default) — button always shown beside the title
                    'slide'           — button grows in on hover / focus and
                                        pushes the title, which truncates further
  - data-opc-price  'hidden' — no price line
  - data-opc-compare 'hidden' — no compare-at price
  - data-opc-icon   'mask' — the button icon is the image in --opc-cart-icon,
                    drawn as a mask in the button's text colour (built-in icons
                    and merchant uploads alike); without it the bag is inline
  Price type comes from --opc-price-size and --opc-price-weight. The card
  colour is --opc-plate-bg / --opc-plate-fg (and --opc-cart-bg / --opc-cart-fg
  for the button): unset, the scheme's surface and heading colour; a composer
  set to Accent publishes the scheme's neutral accent and its contrast. A
  glass plate's look is --opc-glass-bg / -filter / -edge / -fallback
  (snippets/glass-resolver), a floating plate's corners --opc-plate-radius.
  Set each one in one place only (card or ancestor), never both. Shape comes
  from --opc-ratio — always a fixed ratio (the composing block's "Card shape"
  1:1 / 4:5 / 3:4 / 2:3 / 4:3 / 3:2 / 16:9); there is no natural-height mode.

  The add to cart button is a PLACEHOLDER: it renders and animates but is not
  wired to the cart yet, so it is marked aria-disabled.

  Accepts:
  - product {Product, optional} blank renders a sample card (theme editor)
  - index   {Number, optional}  1-based position, rotates placeholder artwork
  - plate   {String, optional}  'tint' | 'glass' — sets data-opc-plate here
  - cart    {String, optional}  'fixed' | 'slide' — sets data-opc-cart here
  - price   {Boolean, optional} false hides the price here
  - skeleton {Boolean, optional} true renders the loading placeholder instead:
            the same box, ratio and plate with shimmering bars, no link and no
            product. Used inside a composer's skeleton <template>.

  Schema: none (the composing blocks own the look).

  Usage:
    {% render 'collection-product-card', product: product, index: forloop.index %}
    {% render 'collection-product-card', skeleton: true %}
  Styles: this snippet's stylesheet tag, compiled once into the theme stylesheet.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ==========================================================================
 * Collection Product Card (`opc-`) — snippets/collection-product-card.liquid
 * For the collection sections only (Featured Collection, Collection Tabs,
 * Category Collections); their shells load this file. The card is always a
 * fixed ratio, --opc-ratio, set per breakpoint by the composing block.
 *
 * The image fills the card and a plate carrying the title, the price and an
 * add to cart button sits over its lower edge. Every variant is a data
 * attribute that may live on the card OR on any ancestor, so a parent block can
 * style cards a child block renders; each variant selector therefore matches
 * both places through :is(). Defaults (no attribute): tint plate, edge to edge,
 * fixed button, inline bag icon, price and compare-at price shown.
 *
 * Surfaces follow the card contract: Design System item radius, border and
 * shadow per breakpoint. Every plate (tint, glass, solid) is built from ONE
 * colour pair, --opc-plate-bg / --opc-plate-fg. Unset, that is the scheme's
 * Surface with its heading colour. The composer's "Card colour" Accent
 * publishes the scheme's neutral accent and its contrast colour instead,
 * plus an inverted --opc-cart-bg / --opc-cart-fg. A glass plate's look is
 * --opc-glass-bg / -filter / -edge / -fallback (snippets/glass-resolver.liquid)
 * and a floating plate's corners --opc-plate-radius.
 *
 * SKELETON (.opc-card--skeleton) is the loading placeholder: the same box,
 * ratio and plate, with a shimmer sweeping the surface and bars in the plate's
 * text colour where the title, price and button will be.
 * ========================================================================== */

.opc-card {
  --opc-pad: clamp(0.75rem, 4%, 1.125rem);
  --opc-float-gap: clamp(0.5rem, 3%, 0.75rem);
  --opc-cart-size: 2.5rem;
  --opc-ease: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1);
  position: relative;
  display: block;
  /* The height is width x ratio and nothing else: no percentage height (which
     a stretched slide or grid cell would resolve and let win over the ratio)
     and no in-flow content (media and plate are both absolute), so an image's
     natural size can never give a card its own height. */
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 0;
  aspect-ratio: var(--opc-ratio, 4 / 5);
  overflow: hidden;
  isolation: isolate;
  border: var(--ds-item-border-width-mobile, 0) solid var(--color-border);
  border-radius: var(--ds-item-radius-mobile);
  box-shadow: var(--ds-item-shadow-mobile, none);
  background-color: var(--color-surface);
  color: var(--color-heading);
}

.opc-card__hit {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 1;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ media */

.opc-card__media {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
}

.opc-card__image {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  transition: transform 0.6s var(--opc-ease);
}

.opc-card__image--placeholder {
  fill: var(--color-text);
  opacity: 0.5;
}

.opc-card:hover .opc-card__image {
  transform: scale(1.04);
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ plate */

/* Tint (default): the card colour rising from the bottom edge as a shade. */
.opc-card__plate {
  position: absolute;
  inset: auto 0 0;
  z-index: 2;
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  padding: calc(var(--opc-pad) * 3) var(--opc-pad) var(--opc-pad);
  /* The plate never blocks the card link; only its controls take the pointer. */
  pointer-events: none;
  color: var(--opc-plate-fg, var(--color-heading));
  background: linear-gradient(
    to top,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--opc-plate-bg, var(--color-surface)) 78%, transparent) 0%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--opc-plate-bg, var(--color-surface)) 40%, transparent) 55%,
    transparent 100%
  );
}

/* Glass: rounded top corners, no border. The look comes from the composer
   through snippets/glass-resolver.liquid (--opc-glass-bg / -filter / -edge /
   -fallback): Frosted or Liquid, Touch or Full. Unset, it is the reference
   frosted pane — heavy blur, a soft brightening wash, no edge light. */
:is([data-opc-plate='glass'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-plate='glass']) .opc-card__plate {
  padding-top: var(--opc-pad);
  border-radius: max(12px, var(--ds-item-radius-mobile)) max(12px, var(--ds-item-radius-mobile)) 0 0;
  color: var(--opc-plate-fg, var(--color-heading));
  background: var(--opc-glass-bg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--opc-plate-bg, var(--color-surface)) 28%, transparent));
  box-shadow: var(--opc-glass-edge, none);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--opc-glass-filter, blur(22px) saturate(115%) brightness(1.12));
  backdrop-filter: var(--opc-glass-filter, blur(22px) saturate(115%) brightness(1.12));
}

@supports not ((backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) or (-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px))) {
  :is([data-opc-plate='glass'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-plate='glass']) .opc-card__plate {
    background: var(--opc-glass-fallback, color-mix(in srgb, var(--opc-plate-bg, var(--color-surface)) 88%, transparent));
  }
}

/* Solid: the card colour. It only ever floats (below). */
:is([data-opc-plate='solid'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-plate='solid']) .opc-card__plate {
  padding-top: var(--opc-pad);
  color: var(--opc-plate-fg, var(--color-heading));
  background: var(--opc-plate-bg, var(--color-surface));
}

/* Floating: inset from the card's edges with its own corners — opt-in for
   glass, automatic for solid. --opc-plate-radius is the merchant's corner
   size; unset, the card radius less the inset. */
:is(
    [data-opc-float] .opc-card,
    .opc-card[data-opc-float],
    [data-opc-plate='solid'] .opc-card,
    .opc-card[data-opc-plate='solid']
  )
  .opc-card__plate {
  inset: auto var(--opc-float-gap) var(--opc-float-gap);
  border-radius: var(--opc-plate-radius, max(6px, calc(var(--ds-item-radius-mobile) - var(--opc-float-gap))));
}

.opc-card__text {
  display: flex;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

/* One line, cut with an ellipsis: a button sliding in narrows the text box,
   so the title truncates further instead of jumping to a new line. */
.opc-card__title {
  display: block;
  margin: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  font-family: var(--font-heading-family, inherit);
  font-size: var(--fs-text-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.25;
  color: inherit;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

.opc-card__link {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
  pointer-events: auto;
}

.opc-card__link:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid currentColor;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ price */

.opc-card__price {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  font-size: var(--opc-price-size, var(--fs-text-sm));
  font-weight: var(--opc-price-weight, 400);
  line-height: 1.3;
  opacity: 0.9;
}

.opc-card__compare {
  font-size: 0.85em;
  font-weight: 400;
  opacity: 0.7;
}

:is([data-opc-price='hidden'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-price='hidden']) .opc-card__price,
:is([data-opc-compare='hidden'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-compare='hidden']) .opc-card__compare {
  display: none;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------ add to cart */

.opc-card__cart {
  display: inline-grid;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  place-items: center;
  width: var(--opc-cart-size);
  height: var(--opc-cart-size);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background-color: var(--opc-cart-bg, var(--color-button, var(--color-base)));
  color: var(--opc-cart-fg, var(--color-button-text, var(--color-heading)));
  cursor: pointer;
  pointer-events: auto;
  transition: transform 0.4s var(--opc-ease), opacity 0.3s ease;
}

.opc-card__cart-icon {
  display: block;
  width: 1.15rem;
  height: 1.15rem;
}

.opc-card__cart-icon svg {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

/* A chosen icon (built-in or uploaded) is drawn as a mask in the button's text
   colour, so any upload reads as an icon rather than a picture. */
:is([data-opc-icon='mask'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-icon='mask']) .opc-card__cart-icon {
  background-color: currentColor;
  -webkit-mask: var(--opc-cart-icon) center / contain no-repeat;
  mask: var(--opc-cart-icon) center / contain no-repeat;
}

:is([data-opc-icon='mask'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-icon='mask']) .opc-card__cart-icon svg {
  display: none;
}

.opc-card__cart:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid currentColor;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* Slide: the button grows in on hover or keyboard focus and pushes the title
   along. Closed, it has no width and its flex gap is cancelled, so the title
   uses the whole plate; as width and margin animate (real layout, like the
   collection card's arrow) the one-line title truncates further instead of
   wrapping, and the icon scales and fades in. */
:is([data-opc-cart='slide'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-cart='slide']) .opc-card__cart {
  width: 0;
  margin-inline-start: -0.75rem;
  overflow: hidden;
  opacity: 0;
  transform: scale(0.6);
  transition:
    width 0.4s var(--opc-ease),
    margin 0.4s var(--opc-ease),
    opacity 0.3s ease,
    transform 0.4s var(--opc-ease);
}

:is([data-opc-cart='slide'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-cart='slide']):is(:hover, :focus-within) .opc-card__cart {
  width: var(--opc-cart-size);
  margin-inline-start: 0;
  opacity: 1;
  transform: none;
}

/* No hover on touch screens: the button simply stays in place. */
@media (hover: none) {
  :is([data-opc-cart='slide'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-cart='slide']) .opc-card__cart {
    width: var(--opc-cart-size);
    margin-inline-start: 0;
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------- skeleton */

.opc-card--skeleton::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 1;
  background: linear-gradient(
    100deg,
    transparent 20%,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-base) 55%, transparent) 50%,
    transparent 80%
  );
  transform: translateX(-100%);
  animation: opc-shimmer 1.4s ease-in-out infinite;
}

.opc-skel {
  display: block;
  height: 0.85em;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 24%, transparent);
}

.opc-skel--title {
  width: 80%;
  font-size: var(--fs-text-sm);
}

.opc-skel--short {
  width: 50%;
}

.opc-skel--price {
  width: 3.5em;
  height: 0.75em;
}

/* Bars size against the text column, so it takes the free width at once. */
.opc-card--skeleton .opc-card__text {
  flex-basis: 0;
}

/* The button placeholder is a bar in the plate's text colour, not a button. */
.opc-card--skeleton .opc-card__cart {
  color: inherit;
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 24%, transparent);
  cursor: default;
}

@keyframes opc-shimmer {
  to {
    transform: translateX(100%);
  }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .opc-card__image,
  .opc-card__cart,
  :is([data-opc-cart='slide'] .opc-card, .opc-card[data-opc-cart='slide']) .opc-card__cart {
    transition: none;
  }

  .opc-card--skeleton::before {
    animation: none;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .opc-card:hover .opc-card__image {
    transform: none;
  }
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .opc-card {
    border-width: var(--ds-item-border-width-desktop, 0);
    border-radius: var(--ds-item-radius-desktop);
    box-shadow: var(--ds-item-shadow-desktop, none);
  }

  :is(
      [data-opc-float] .opc-card,
      .opc-card[data-opc-float],
      [data-opc-plate='solid'] .opc-card,
      .opc-card[data-opc-plate='solid']
    )
    .opc-card__plate {
    border-radius: var(--opc-plate-radius, max(6px, calc(var(--ds-item-radius-desktop) - var(--opc-float-gap))));
  }

  .opc-card__title {
    font-size: var(--fs-text-md);
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{%- if skeleton -%}
  <div class="opc-card opc-card--skeleton" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="opc-card__plate">
      <div class="opc-card__text">
        <span class="opc-skel opc-skel--title"></span>
        <span class="opc-skel opc-skel--title opc-skel--short"></span>
        <span class="opc-card__price"><span class="opc-skel opc-skel--price"></span></span>
      </div>
      <span class="opc-card__cart opc-skel--cart"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- else -%}

{%- liquid
  assign opc_index = index | default: 1
  assign ph_index = opc_index | minus: 1 | modulo: 6 | plus: 1
  assign ph_name = 'product-' | append: ph_index

  if product != blank
    assign opc_title = product.title | escape
    assign opc_url = product.url
  else
    assign opc_title = 'onboarding.product_title' | t | append: ' ' | append: opc_index
    assign opc_url = blank
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="opc-card{% if product == blank %} opc-card--sample{% endif %}"
  {% if plate != blank %}data-opc-plate="{{ plate }}"{% endif %}
  {% if cart != blank %}data-opc-cart="{{ cart }}"{% endif %}
  {% if price == false %}data-opc-price="hidden"{% endif %}
>
  {%- if opc_url != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%} Whole-card hit area; the title link is the accessible one. {%- endcomment -%}
    <a class="opc-card__hit" href="{{ opc_url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></a>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="opc-card__media">
    {%- if product != blank and product.featured_image != blank -%}
      {{
        product.featured_image
        | image_url: width: 900
        | image_tag:
          class: 'opc-card__image',
          loading: 'lazy',
          widths: '300,450,600,750,900',
          sizes: '(min-width: 768px) 25vw, 60vw',
          alt: product.featured_image.alt
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ ph_name | placeholder_svg_tag: 'opc-card__image opc-card__image--placeholder' }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="opc-card__plate">
    <div class="opc-card__text">
      <h3 class="opc-card__title">
        {%- if opc_url != blank -%}
          <a class="opc-card__link" href="{{ opc_url }}">{{ opc_title }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ opc_title }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </h3>
      <span class="opc-card__price">
        {%- if product != blank -%}
          {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
            <s class="opc-card__compare">{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span>{{ product.price | money }}</span>
        {%- else -%}
          <span>{{ 2900 | money }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Placeholder: not wired to the cart yet. {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="opc-card__cart"
      data-opc-cart-button
      aria-disabled="true"
      aria-label="{{ 'theme.components.product_card.add_to_cart' | t: title: opc_title }}"
    >
      <span class="opc-card__cart-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        {{- 'icon-bag.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}
